      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-24T04:55:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"peterrecore\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b77776/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> peterrecore:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In general, how can we tell what tokens created by powers are removed with their card and which stay? &nbsp;Is there errata for Impaling Structures or is there a general rule I am missing? &nbsp;For example, Citizen Dawn's \"Return with the Dawn\" specifically mentions that the Citizen is removed when the card is removed, but Impaling does not.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>All tokens that are generated by cards are removed from play when the associated card is removed from play.</p>",
